@startuml
!include ../_style.puml
title Design - administration pages
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Permission-aware page tabs" as Tabs
rectangle "Settings\nNative site policy form" as Settings
rectangle "Profiles\nNamed profile cards" as Profiles
rectangle "Migrations\nProfile, rules and editions" as Migrations
rectangle "Log\nAction and reference filters" as Log
rectangle "Profile editor\nUnsaved rule preview / save" as Editor
rectangle "Stored migration review\nCounts / grouped files / decision filters" as Review
rectangle "Execution\nConfirmation / maintenance / progress" as Execution
Tabs --> Settings
Tabs --> Profiles
Tabs --> Migrations
Tabs --> Log
Profiles --> Editor
Migrations --> Review
Review --> Execution
note bottom of Tabs
Every route checks its own capability.
Course pages use separate course tabs.
end note
@enduml
